# FR-R3-090 (SUP-01) — third-party lifecycle scripts do not run on install, by
# default rather than by a contributor remembering a flag.
#
# This file is the only authority on how the repository installs. The hardening
# used to live in the workflow files as `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, so the tree CI
# scanned was installed differently from the tree a contributor ran — the
# contributor's being the less hardened of the two, on the machine that runs an
# uncontained agent CLI. Actions were retired on 2026-08-26 by operator decision
# (`FR-R3-099`) and those files were deleted, so the dual authority is gone
# rather than reconciled, and there is no remote install left to match.
#
# WHAT THIS BREAKS, and it is this repository's own script rather than a
# dependency's: package.json declares
#   "postinstall": "npm --prefix webview-ui install --no-audit --no-fund"
# With scripts off it no longer runs, so `webview-ui/node_modules` is not
# populated by `npm ci` alone. That is not a regression to work around — the
# hardened install has always worked this way and compensates with an explicit
# second install. The same explicit command is a DECLARED step in
# CONTRIBUTING.md, per the FR-R3-065 rule that a prerequisite hidden inside a
# gate is not the same as a declared one.
#
# tests/lint/install-flag-parity.test.ts reads this file and the documents that
# teach the install sequence, and fails if they disagree — or if a workflow
# directory reappears to become a second authority again.
ignore-scripts=true
